e pointer that\n2697:       was set in the variable length string datatype for the attribute.  That file\n2698:       pointer was already closed when the attribute was accessed.\n2699: \n2700:       The problem was fixed by setting the file pointer to the current opened file pointer\n2701:       when the attribute was accessed.  Similar patch up was done before when reading\n--- 2717\n2705: \n2706:     - Fixed CVE-2020-10810\n2707: \n2708:       The tool h5clear produced a segfault during an error recovery in\n2709:       the superblock decoding.  An internal pointer was reset to prevent\n2710:       further accessing when it is not assigned with a value.\n2711: \n2712:       (BMR - 2020/06/29, HDFFV-11053)\n2713: \n2714:     - Fixed CVE-2018-17435\n2715: \n2716:       The tool h52gif produced a segfault when the size of an attribute\n2717:       message was corrupted and caused a buffer overflow.\n2718: \n2719:       The problem was fixed by verifying the attribute message's size\n2720:       against the buffer size before accessing the buffer.  h52gif was\n2721:       also fixed to display the failure instead of silently exiting\n2722:       after the segfault was eliminated.\n2723: \n2724:       (BMR - 2020/06/19, HDFFV-10591)\n2725: \n2726: \n2727:     Java Library\n2728:     ------------\n2729:     - JNI utility function does not handle new references.\n2730: \n2731:       The JNI utility function for converting reference data to string did\n2732:       not use the new APIs. In addition to fixing that function, added new\n2733:       java tests for using the new APIs.\n2734: \n2735:       (ADB - 2021/02/16, HDFFV-11212)\n--- 474\n462: The lib folder contains the library files, and CMake adds the pkgconfig\n463: subfolder with the hdf5*.pc files used by the bin/build scripts created by\n464: the CMake build. CMake separates the C interface code from the fortran code by\n465: creating C-stub libraries for each Fortran library. In addition, only CMake\n466: installs the tools library. The names of the szip libraries are different\n467: between the build systems.\n468: \n469: The share folder will have the most differences because CMake builds include\n470: a number of CMake specific files for support of CMake's find_package and support\n471: for the HDF5 Examples CMake project.\n472: \n473: The issues with the gif tool are:\n474:     HDFFV-10592 CVE-2018-17433\n475:     HDFFV-10593 CVE-2018-17436\n476:     HDFFV-11048 CVE-2020-10809\n477: These CVE issues have not yet been addressed and can be avoided by not building\n478: the gif tool. Disable building the High-Level tools with these options:\n479:     autotools:   --disable-hltools\n480:     cmake:       HDF5_BUILD_HL_TOOLS=OFF\n481: \n482: \n483: %%%%1.13.2%%%%\n484: \n485: HDF5 version 1.13.2 released on 2022-08-15\n486: ================================================================================\n487: \n488: \n489: INTRODUCTION\n490: ============\n491: \n492: This document describes the differences between this release and the previous\n--- 526\n514: \n515:      help@hdfgroup.org\n516: \n517: \n518: CONTENTS\n519: ========\n520: \n521: - New Features\n522: - Support for new platforms and languages\n523: - Bug Fixes since HDF5-1.13.1\n524: - Platforms Tested\n525: - Known Problems\n526: - CMake vs. Autotools installations\n527: \n528: \n529: New Features\n530: ============\n531: \n532:     Configuration:\n533:     -------------\n534:     - Correct the usage of CMAKE_Fortran_MODULE_DIRECTORY and where to\n535:       install Fortran mod files.\n536: \n537:       The Fortran modules files, ending in .mod are files describing a\n538:       Fortran 90 (and above) module API and ABI. These are not like C\n539:       header files describing an API, they are compiler dependent and\n540:       arch dependent, and not easily readable by a human being. They are\n541:       nevertheless searched for in the includes directories by gfortran\n542:       (in directories specified wi